    "paper\\en\\manuscript\\FAECO.tex": [
      {
        "line": 267,
        "text": "The single-round study evaluates repair quality and efficiency. Figure~\\ref{fig:iscas_main} compares baseline and repaired ISCAS89 netlists; all eight improve strictly under ideal-net OpenSTA. R/G/B/JOINT constructions preserve flip-flops, clock and reset logic. All final pairs pass independent SEC (Table~\\ref{tab:sec_iscas8}). Accepted candidate types are JOINT for s27/s382/s420/s953, G for s641/s713/s832, and R for s820; no standalone B candidate is accepted. This is the efficiency-first configuration\\label{sec:eff_prio}, with the 10\\,ps physical gate disabled. Thus s420's +0.01\\,ns candidate is accepted under $\\Delta\\mathrm{WNS}>0$. The stopping condition differs from the subsequent multi-round study, so results are reported separately. JOINT combines local implementation and drive changes; G changes drive strength; R depends on equivalent Boolean implementations available in the library."
      },
